slftp REST API Documentation (Beta)
Status: Early beta; Windows untested. Only the endpoints below are functional; all others are currently stubbed and are not documented.

Base URL
- http://<host>:<port>/api (default http://127.0.0.1:8089/api)
- Calls are POST to /api/<Interface>/<Method> with JSON bodies; responses often wrap data in result: [ ... ].

Authentication
- If apikey is set in config/slftp.ini, send Authorization: Bearer <key>.
- If apikey is empty, no auth required (not recommended on exposed hosts).
- API key protection only applies to /api/* paths; web UI is served without auth.

Implemented Endpoints

System
- ApiSystemService.GetStatus
  POST /api/ApiSystemService/GetStatus
  Returns Version, Uptime, SitesCount/Up/Down, QueueSize, ActiveTasks.
  Example: curl -X POST -H "Authorization: Bearer <key>" http://127.0.0.1:8089/api/ApiSystemService/GetStatus

- ApiSystemService.GetUptime
  POST /api/ApiSystemService/GetUptime
  Returns uptime in seconds.

- ApiSystemService.GetVersion
  POST /api/ApiSystemService/GetVersion
  Returns version string.

- ApiSystemService.Shutdown
  POST /api/ApiSystemService/Shutdown
  Initiates graceful shutdown of slftp. Use with caution!

- ApiSystemService.GetRecentReleases
  POST /api/ApiSystemService/GetRecentReleases
  Body: {"Limit": 20}
  Returns recent releases with basic info (name, section, sites, queue number, status).
  Response includes: ReleaseName, Section, Added (Unix timestamp), PazoId, Ready, Stopped, QueueNumber, Sites (array).

- ApiSystemService.GetReleaseDetails
  POST /api/ApiSystemService/GetReleaseDetails
  Body: {"PazoId": <id>}
  Returns detailed information for a specific release including per-site progress.
  Response includes: ReleaseName, Section, TotalFiles, Ready, Stopped, QueueNumber, ErrorReason,
  and SiteDetails (array with: SiteName, Complete, FileCount, TotalFiles, FilesRacedByMe, Percent, Status).

Sites
- ApiSitesService.GetSites
  POST /api/ApiSitesService/GetSites
  Body: {"Filter":""} to list all sites. Returns counts and a Sites field (JSON array or JSON string).
  Example: curl -X POST -H "Authorization: Bearer <key>" -H "Content-Type: application/json" -d '{"Filter":""}' http://127.0.0.1:8089/api/ApiSitesService/GetSites

- ApiSitesService.GetSite
  POST /api/ApiSitesService/GetSite
  Body: {"SiteName":"<name>"}
  Returns details for a specific site.

- Mutating endpoints (live changes):
  - Set max up/down: POST /api/ApiSitesService/SetSiteMaxUpDn with {"SiteName":"<name>","MaxUp":<int>,"MaxDn":<int>}
  - Set slots: POST /api/ApiSitesService/SetSiteSlots with {"SiteName":"<name>","Slots":<int>}
  - Set max pre-queue: POST /api/ApiSitesService/SetSiteMaxPreDn with {"SiteName":"<name>","MaxPreDn":<int>}
  - Set status (UP/DOWN): POST /api/ApiSitesService/SetSiteStatus with {"SiteName":"<name>","Status":"UP|DOWN"}
  - Set perm down: POST /api/ApiSitesService/SetSitePermDown with {"SiteName":"<name>","PermDown":true|false}
  - Set autologin: POST /api/ApiSitesService/SetSiteAutoLogin with {"SiteName":"<name>","Enabled":true|false}
  - Set autorules interval: POST /api/ApiSitesService/SetSiteAutoRules with {"SiteName":"<name>","IntervalSeconds":<int>}
  - Run autorules now: POST /api/ApiSitesService/RunSiteAutoRules with {"SiteName":"<name>"}
  - Test site (enqueue login): POST /api/ApiSitesService/TestSite with {"SiteName":"<name>"}
  - Ghost kill: POST /api/ApiSitesService/GhostSite with {"SiteName":"<name>"}
  - Recalc freeslots: POST /api/ApiSitesService/RecalcFreeSlots with {"SiteName":"<name>"}
  - Rebuild slots: POST /api/ApiSitesService.RebuildSlots with {"SiteName":"<name>"}
  These calls modify runtime state; use with caution.

Queue
- ApiQueueService.GetQueueStats
  POST /api/ApiQueueService/GetQueueStats
  Body: {"SiteName":""}
  Returns TotalTasks, RaceTasks, DirlistTasks, AutoTasks, OtherTasks.

Web UI
- The Web UI is served at http://<host>:<port>/ (default http://127.0.0.1:8089/)
- Built with React + Mantine UI v8
- Features: Dashboard with recent releases, Site manager, Release details modal
- No authentication required for web UI (only for /api/* endpoints)
- TODO: Authentication for Web UI is not yet implemented

Everything else
- Stats, IRC, Rules, Speed, KnowledgeBase, Precatcher, Task creation endpoints are currently stubbed (empty placeholders) and are intentionally not documented here until implemented.
